You need to adjust your HTML and CSS to properly align the Spotify logo and text. Try this:  

### **✅ Solution Using Flexbox**
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Spotify Navbar</title>
    <style>
        .navbar {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            background-color: black;
            padding: 10px;
        }
        .navbar img {
            width: 40px; /* Adjust size */
            height: auto;
            margin-right: 10px; /* Space between logo and text */
        }
        .navbar .brand {
            color: white;
            font-size: 20px;
            font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="navbar">
        <img src="spotify-logo.png" alt="Spotify Logo">
        <span class="brand">Spotify</span>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
```

### **🔥 Why This Works?**  
✅ **`display: flex;`** aligns items horizontally.  
✅ **`align-items: center;`** keeps the logo and text aligned.  
✅ **`margin-right: 10px;`** adds spacing between the logo and text.  

