### **📌 Padding in CSS**
**Padding** is the space **inside** an element, between its content and the border. It creates **internal spacing** inside elements.

### **1️⃣ Basic Syntax**
```css
element {
    padding: 10px;  /* Adds 10px space on all sides */
}
```

### **2️⃣ Padding on Specific Sides**
```css
element {
    padding-top: 10px;    /* Top padding */
    padding-right: 15px;  /* Right padding */
    padding-bottom: 20px; /* Bottom padding */
    padding-left: 25px;   /* Left padding */
}
```

### **3️⃣ Shorthand Padding (Clockwise Order)**
```css
padding: 10px 20px 30px 40px;  
/* Top | Right | Bottom | Left */
```
👉 Example:  
```css
padding: 10px 20px;  
/* Top & Bottom | Left & Right */
```

### **4️⃣ Auto & Percentage Values**
- `padding: auto;` **(NOT valid, padding does not support auto)**
- `padding: 10%;` **(10% of the parent element’s width)**

### **5️⃣ Padding Example**
```css
.box {
    background: lightblue;
    padding: 20px;
    border: 2px solid black;
}
```
🔹 This adds **20px of space inside** the `.box`, pushing the content away from the border.

